<title>INDIA: India gold, silver fall on weaker world prices.</title>
<headline>India gold, silver fall on weaker world prices.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold and silver prices were dragged down on Tuesday by fresh arrivals and the weak trend in world markets, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices of a gold biscuit (116.50 gramme) fell 300 rupees to 58,800 per piece, after losing 350 rupees on Monday and 650 rupees last week.</p>
<p>Traders said talk that the government may liberalise gold imports also undermined the sentiment.</p>
<p>Buyers kept to the sidelines awaiting a further decline in prices ahead of the approaching wedding season, they said.  </p>
